"video": "",
"content": "This section addresses WAEC Agricultural Science Paper 3 (Practical Test or Alternative to Practical Paper - ATTP).\n\nContent (Reflecting typical WAEC practicals/ATTP scenarios):\n\nSpecimen Identification and Description: Identifying common crop plants, livestock breeds, farm tools, pests, disease symptoms, soil samples, fertilizers from diagrams, pictures, or descriptions. Stating characteristics or uses.\n\nExperimental Procedures and Setups: Questions based on diagrams of experimental setups (e.g., for soil tests, germination tests, photosynthesis experiments, simple animal anatomy). Identifying apparatus, stating functions, outlining procedures, stating precautions.\n\nData Handling and Interpretation: Recording \"mock\" experimental data, completing tables, plotting simple graphs (e.g., growth rates, yield responses), interpreting results, drawing conclusions.\n\nFarm Management Calculations: Simple calculations related to feed rations, fertilizer application rates, plant population, yield estimation.\n\nAgricultural Practices: Describing how to carry out specific farm operations (e.g., planting, grafting, castration, feed preparation).\n\nATTP Question Formats:\n\nInterpreting diagrams, photographs, or scenarios.\n\nAnswering structured questions based on provided information.\n\nDesigning a simple experiment (stating aim, materials, brief procedure, expected results, precautions).\n\nModel Answers and Guidance: Provide detailed answers for ATTP questions, showing how to interpret information, present observations, perform calculations, and draw logical conclusions based on scientific agricultural principles.\n\nThe goal of this chapter is to give students robust, exam-focused practice specifically tailored to WAEC Agricultural Science expectations.",
